    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0736" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/8–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-23T19:00:00-03:00">August 23, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 24—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2641. For Department and Freedman, FEA.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d575-f1"/>
                    Department’s telegram 2047, August 22.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d575-f2"/> Foreign
                    Office informally but authoritatively states Brazil unconditionally accepts
                    liquidation of Decentralization Plan of export control. Formal note to this
                    effect is to be delivered by 25th. It is believed public announcement may safely
                    be made on basis of assurance received from office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d575-f1" n="16" xml:id="d575-f1-content">
                <p>Walter Freedman, Acting Director, Requirements and Supply Branch, Bureau of
                    Supplies, Foreign Economic Administration.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d575-f2" n="17" xml:id="d575-f2-content">
